From: Magnus Reimann <magnus.reimann@mailbox.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:24:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH rumpkernel] bus_dma: use machine addresses for boundaries and coalescing

Hello,

This is a patch for Debian's rumpkernel package (to add to
debian/patches, after rump_bus_dma).  It fixes the
"pciide_dma: ... not properly aligned / panic: pciide_dma: buf align"
panic of rumpdisk, and more importantly DMA segments that point to
machine pages not belonging to the buffer.  Details are in the
description below.

A self-contained test harness (old and new function against a mock
virt_to_mach) is at
https://github.com/MevPR/mach-SMP/blob/main/smp-dev/outbox/rumpkernel/busdma_test.c
I could not rebuild the rumpkernel package itself to test it on a
running system.

This work was done together with Claude (an AI model by Anthropic).

---
Description: bus_dma: use machine addresses for boundaries and coalescing
 _bus_dmamap_load_buffer gets the host virtual address of each chunk
 (vtophys is the identity in rump) and only converts it to a machine
 address with rumpcomp_pci_virt_to_mach for the segment start.  The
 boundary check was however done on the virtual address, and chunks were
 coalesced when they were contiguous in virtual memory and their machine
 addresses fell in the same boundary-sized block.  Pages that are
 contiguous in virtual memory are not necessarily so in machine memory,
 so a segment could cover the wrong machine pages: the device then
 transfers to or from memory that does not belong to the buffer.  When
 the bogus segment happens to cross a 64KiB boundary, pciide catches it:
 .
   pciide_dma: seg 0 addr 0x7976f200 len 0x1800 not properly aligned
   panic: pciide_dma: buf align
 .
 (seen with rumpdisk on Debian GNU/Hurd amd64); otherwise the transfer
 silently goes to the wrong pages.
 .
 Get the machine address of each chunk once, apply the boundary to it,
 and only coalesce chunks that are contiguous in machine memory.
 .
 A test harness running the old and the new function on 200000 random
 buffers whose pages are partly contiguous, partly scattered in machine
 memory: the old code produced a wrong mapping for 14630 of them and a
 segment crossing 64KiB for 1873, the new code for none.
Author: Magnus Reimann <magnus.reimann@mailbox.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

--- rumpkernel.orig/buildrump.sh/src/sys/rump/dev/lib/libpci/rumpdev_bus_dma.c	2026-11-25 20:22:31
+++ rumpkernel/buildrump.sh/src/sys/rump/dev/lib/libpci/rumpdev_bus_dma.c	2026-11-25 20:23:11
@@ -158,7 +158,7 @@
 	bus_addr_t *lastaddrp, int *segp, int first)
 {
 	bus_size_t sgsize;
-	bus_addr_t curaddr, lastaddr, baddr, bmask;
+	bus_addr_t curaddr, lastaddr, baddr, bmask, maddr;
 	vaddr_t vaddr = (vaddr_t)buf;
 	int seg;
 
@@ -187,6 +187,14 @@
 			return (EINVAL);
 
 		/*
+		 * CURADDR is a host virtual address: the device needs the
+		 * machine address, and that is also what boundaries and
+		 * contiguity are about, since pages that are contiguous in
+		 * virtual memory need not be in machine memory.
+		 */
+		maddr = rumpcomp_pci_virt_to_mach((void *)curaddr);
+
+		/*
 		 * Compute the segment size, and adjust counts.
 		 */
 		sgsize = PAGE_SIZE - ((u_long)vaddr & PGOFSET);
@@ -198,9 +206,9 @@
 		 * Make sure we don't cross any boundaries.
 		 */
 		if (map->_dm_boundary > 0) {
-			baddr = (curaddr + map->_dm_boundary) & bmask;
-			if (sgsize > (baddr - curaddr))
-				sgsize = (baddr - curaddr);
+			baddr = (maddr + map->_dm_boundary) & bmask;
+			if (sgsize > (baddr - maddr))
+				sgsize = (baddr - maddr);
 		}
 
 		/*
@@ -208,23 +216,22 @@
 		 * the previous segment if possible.
 		 */
 		if (first) {
-			map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr
-			    = rumpcomp_pci_virt_to_mach((void *)curaddr);
+			map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr = maddr;
 			map->dm_segs[seg].ds_len = sgsize;
 			first = 0;
 		} else {
-			if (curaddr == lastaddr &&
+			if (maddr == map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr +
+			     map->dm_segs[seg].ds_len &&
 			    (map->dm_segs[seg].ds_len + sgsize) <=
 			     map->dm_maxsegsz &&
 			    (map->_dm_boundary == 0 ||
 			     (map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr & bmask) ==
-			     (rumpcomp_pci_virt_to_mach((void*)curaddr)&bmask)))
+			     (maddr & bmask)))
 				map->dm_segs[seg].ds_len += sgsize;
 			else {
 				if (++seg >= map->_dm_segcnt)
 					break;
-				map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr =
-				    rumpcomp_pci_virt_to_mach((void *)curaddr);
+				map->dm_segs[seg].ds_addr = maddr;
 				map->dm_segs[seg].ds_len = sgsize;
 			}
 		}
